---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/guides/flow-collision-prevention";
const title = "Shopify email flow collision prevention";
const desc = "Decide which message may leave the queue for Shopify lifecycle email with explicit owners, proposed exercises and reversible decisions.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does cart always outrank welcome?",
    "answer": "Choose precedence around customer intent and existing promises. A cart reminder can replace a redundant promotion while the promised signup benefit remains accessible."
  },
  {
    "question": "Are tags enough?",
    "answer": "Only if their ownership, timing, versioning and queue cancellation behavior meet the policy. Demonstrate stale updates and dispatch-time checks."
  },
  {
    "question": "When should we review the matrix?",
    "answer": "Review affected pairs whenever a sender, offer, integration or eligibility rule changes, and assign a recurring owner based on your operating risk."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/guides">Operator guides</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Decide which message may leave the queue</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Decide which message may leave the queue for Shopify lifecycle email with explicit owners, proposed exercises and reversible decisions.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Register every sender</h2><p>Inventory campaigns, welcome, cart, browse, post-purchase, replenishment, winback, loyalty and review requests, including SMS and third-party apps. Record purpose, trigger, owner, eligibility, delay, offer and cancellation mechanism. A frequency cap limits volume; it does not decide which conflicting promise to honor.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Write a purpose-specific priority matrix</h2><p>For each overlapping pair, choose send, defer, replace or cancel. A cart reminder may replace browse promotion, while promised welcome benefits still need fulfillment. Do not suppress a promised incentive merely because another flow enrolled. Separate essential order notices from promotional post-purchase content and review permissions for each purpose.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Give each journey an identity</h2><p>Use customer, store, triggering object and journey version to distinguish a new cart from a retried event. Record both source event identity and the message decision key. Deduplicating one webhook delivery does not prevent two different applications from deciding to send the same offer.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Make enrollment and release explicit</h2><p>An active-flow flag needs an owner, entry time, expiry policy and terminal reason. Purchase, cart replacement, withdrawal and manual pause can end a journey differently. A delayed exit from an old cart must not clear the active state for a newer cart. Prefer version-aware transitions over an unqualified remove-tag action.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Recheck at dispatch</h2><p>Enrollment eligibility can become stale while a message waits. Recheck permission, purchase state, support holds, inventory and offer availability immediately before dispatch. Define what happens when the latest state is unavailable: hold the promotional message and assign a recovery owner rather than treating missing data as approval.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Coordinate offers across channels</h2><p>Maintain an issued-offer record with code, promise, eligibility and expiry. Agree whether SMS replaces an email touch or adds a distinct service. Channel permission remains separate. Ask each integration supplier to demonstrate propagation delay, cancellation of queued work and behavior when the other system is offline; do not assume a shared tag is instantaneous.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Plan sale overrides and restoration</h2><p>Record the sale start and end, affected branches, checkout combination rules and who restores ordinary logic. Keep reminder and service content available where appropriate. Review already-issued codes before replacing offers. A sale calendar should reflect the actual campaign, rather than a universal November pause date.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Proposed collision exercise</h2><p>In a non-sending environment, simulate signup followed by browse, cart and purchase. Repeat with an out-of-order purchase update, duplicate delivery, reopened support hold and permission withdrawal during a delay. Write expected decisions first, then retain event times, queue actions and reasons. These are proposed exercises, not merchant results.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Investigate an incident from the queue</h2><p>Start with the recipient timeline and message IDs. Distinguish a repeated source event, two independent journeys, a stale eligibility snapshot and a cancellation that arrived after handoff to the sender. Stop the affected promotional branch, reconcile outstanding messages, and record the precise state transition to repair.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Measure the cost of the policy</h2><p>Track suppressed and deferred messages by reason alongside complaints, redemptions, support contacts and contribution after discounts. Fewer messages alone does not establish more profit. Use comparable cohorts or a planned experiment before claiming a revenue effect; include maintenance time and connector charges in operating cost.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12 prose-shopify"><h2>Integration evidence to request</h2><p>For a custom webhook integration, Shopify documents delivery verification and duplicate handling. Ask the integration owner to show how those controls connect to journey state; webhook verification alone does not establish permission to send.</p><p><a class="link" href="https://shopify.dev/docs/apps/build/webhooks/verify-deliveries">Shopify: verify webhook deliveries</a> (reviewed 25 November 2026).</p></section>
  <nav class="container pb-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4" aria-label="Related operating guidance">
    <a class="link" href="/guides/consent-compliance">Consent compliance</a>
    <a class="link" href="/guides/deliverability">Deliverability</a>
    <a class="link" href="/guides/discount-discipline">Discount discipline</a>
    <a class="link" href="/guides/revenue-attribution">Revenue attribution</a>
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">Use-case playbooks</a>
    <a class="link" href="/for">Store-type guides</a>
  </nav>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
